---
description: Git identity, conventional commits, and exec-push constraints
alwaysApply: true
---

- Use default global git user (`git config --global user.name`, `git config --global user.email`)—never cursor/system identity
- Never `--no-verify` or `--trailer` (e.g. Co-authored-by)
- Fix lint, type-check, and test failures before committing
- Conventional Commits: `<type>(<scope>): <short summary>` — type/scope lowercase, summary imperative, ≤60 chars, no period. Scope: app (`next`, `fastify`, `docu`), package (`ui`, `core`, `utils`), or omit
- Branch/validate/commit/push/PR: `/b-exec-push` (read `.agents/skills/b/b-exec-push/SKILL.md`). Commit message: `/b-git-commit`
